WEBVTT

00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:30.025
Or enable a world,
where, you now, there's --

00:06:30.049 --> 00:06:32.316
the main punchline being
that you create a world

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.733
where people make
a life and not just a living.

00:06:34.757 --> 00:06:37.118
AG: That is both incredibly lofty

00:06:37.142 --> 00:06:39.060
and extraordinarily vague.

00:06:39.084 --> 00:06:40.368
What did it mean to you?

00:06:41.861 --> 00:06:45.043
DF: I always really connected
with the aspects of work.

00:06:46.565 --> 00:06:50.980
Not as much the sort of, non-work side,

00:06:51.004 --> 00:06:52.778
however we define that.

00:06:52.802 --> 00:06:55.167
So I thought that was very exciting,

00:06:55.191 --> 00:06:58.706
you know, if I'm an embroidery
designer sending invoices

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.373
and billing is not so
exciting, or signing a lease,